      "tabLabel": "About",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Apples",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Apples is a four-player trick-taking game with bidding, a chosen trump suit, target cards, and scoring from pairs, triples, and four-of-a-kind groups won in tricks."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Apples is documented as a modern standard-deck trick game related in feel to Hearts, Spades, and Bridge, but with its own bid pile and set-scoring system."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Four players each receive thirteen cards before bidding."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Use one standard 52-card deck, ranking ace high."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52-card deck, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal all cards clockwise, then run bidding to set trump and exchange cards through the bidding pile before each player sets a target card aside."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
